@startuml sequence-projects
!theme plain

title Project Management (Local/Mutable)

participant "MCP Client" as Client
participant "Gateway" as Gateway
database "Store" as DB

note over Client, Gateway
  Projects are LOCAL entities.
  They exist only on this gateway
  and are MUTABLE (can be updated/deleted).
  
  Projects help organize work context
  for the MCP client.
end note

== Create Project ==

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/projects\n{name: "My Go Project",\n description: "Learning Go",\n agent_uuid: "my-agent",\n tags: ["golang-uuid", "tutorial-uuid"]}
activate Gateway

Gateway -> Gateway: Generate project ID
Gateway -> Gateway: Set created_at, updated_at

Gateway -> DB: CreateProject(project)
DB --> Gateway: OK
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created\n{project with id}
deactivate Gateway

== List Projects ==

Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/projects?agent_uuid={my-uuid}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: ListProjects(agent_uuid)
DB --> Gateway: [Project, ...]
Gateway --> Client: 200 OK\n[projects]
deactivate Gateway

== Get Project ==

Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/projects/{project-id}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: GetProject(id)
alt Not found
    DB --> Gateway: NotFoundError
    Gateway --> Client: 404 Not Found
else Found
    DB --> Gateway: Project
    Gateway --> Client: 200 OK\n{project}
end
deactivate Gateway

== Update Project ==

Client -> Gateway: PUT /api/v1/projects/{project-id}\n{name: "My Go Project (Updated)",\n description: "Advanced Go",\n tags: ["golang-uuid", "advanced-uuid"]}
activate Gateway

Gateway -> DB: UpdateProject(project)
note right of DB
  Updates: name, description, tags
  Auto-updates: updated_at
end note

alt Not found
    DB --> Gateway: NotFoundError
    Gateway --> Client: 404 Not Found
else Success
    DB --> Gateway: OK
    Gateway --> Client: 200 OK\n{updated project}
end
deactivate Gateway

== Delete Project ==

Client -> Gateway: DELETE /api/v1/projects/{project-id}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: DeleteProject(id)
DB --> Gateway: OK
Gateway --> Client: 204 No Content
deactivate Gateway

== Using Project Context ==

note over Client
  Projects provide context for:
  - Default tags when creating fragments
  - Filtering queries to relevant content
  - Organizing work sessions
end note

Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/projects/{project-id}
Gateway --> Client: {project with default tags}

Client -> Client: Create Fragment with\nproject's default tags

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/fragments\n{fragment with project tags}
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created

== Project vs Session ==

note over Client, Gateway
  Project: Long-lived work context
  - Persists across sessions
  - Contains metadata, default tags
  - Helps organize knowledge
  
  Session: Authentication state
  - Expires after 24 hours
  - Tracks last activity
  - Required for authenticated requests
end note

@enduml
